  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing (NAICS 325412) registered $11.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The market recorded 13,935 awards and an average award size of $855K. Obligations fell 9.0% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer with $11.1B in obligations, leaving other agencies to share the remaining federal spend. McKesson Corporation is the dominant supplier with $11.1B in obligations, followed by several specialty vendors that each account for tens to low hundreds of millions in award value. Historical fiscal-year obligations show wide swings: FY21 was $19.5B, FY22 was $34.4B, FY23 was $12.8B, FY24 was $10.1B, and FY25 was $13.1B. Current-year totals are partial because figures are fiscal year to date. This market remains concentrated on a few large buyers and a small set of high-dollar vendors, with the Department of Veterans Affairs and McKesson Corporation accounting for the largest shares of FY2026 to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is federal buying in NAICS 325412?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $11.1B in FY2026 to date, driving most of the sector's spending. The Department of Health and Human Services is the next-largest buyer with $574M, followed by smaller commitments from agencies such as the Department of Justice with $174M and the Department of Defense with $58.5M. This buyer mix makes the market heavily weighted toward a single agency."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who captures the largest share of contract dollars in NAICS 325412?",
        "body": "MCKESSON CORPORATION received $11.1B in FY2026 to date, making the company the largest vendor by far. EMERGENT BIOSOLUTIONS CANADA INC, EXELAN PHARMACEUTICALS INC, and PHLOW CORP. each received between $105M and $118M, with other top vendors receiving tens of millions. A small group of vendors therefore captures most of the obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
